{{#if ai_enabled}}
## AI chat conventions

The Docsbook AI chat is **enabled** on this site. To make answers citable and accurate:

- Use **`##` (H2) headings** for each distinct concept. The AI uses H2s as citation anchors.
- Put a short factual answer in the **first paragraph** under each H2 — that paragraph is what gets quoted.
- Avoid burying key facts inside long prose; prefer short paragraphs + lists.
- Add a `## FAQ` section near the bottom of long pages with question-style H2/H3s.
{{/if}}

## Docsbook MCP

To manage this workspace from your agent, connect the Docsbook MCP server once:

```
mcp add --transport http https://docsbook.io/api/mcp/server
```

After connecting, the following MCP tools become available:
`get_workspace`, `update_branding`, `update_ui_settings`, `update_navigation`, `update_ai_settings`, `update_seo`, `update_languages`, `get_doc_graph`, `get_analytics`, and more.

## Common `@docs-skills` commands

Install the skills catalog locally with `npx docs-skills install`, then invoke any of these:

- `@docs-skills docs-analyze` — full quality audit of the docs (a11y, SEO, style, structure, links).
- `@docs-skills docs-setup-workspace {{owner}}/{{repo}}` — (re)apply branding, UI, AI, SEO, languages.
- `@docs-skills docs-generate-agents-md {{owner}}/{{repo}}` — regenerate this AGENTS.md from current workspace state.
- `@docs-skills docs-enable-translation` — enable AI auto-translation to additional languages (PRO).
- `@docs-skills docs-tune-ai-chat` — analyze AI chat feedback and propose an improved system prompt (PRO).

